.TH GRIDDEMO 1
.SH NAME
griddemo \- plot pixels snapped to a lattice
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/griddemo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I GridDemo
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Grid.HC
demonstration, whose entry point is
.B GridDemo()
\- the name this port takes, since
.B grid
in section 1 is already
.IR grid-session (1).
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
It is
.IR mousedemo (1)
with the pointer snapped to a five-pixel lattice and the arrow cursor
replaced by a five-pixel square, which is what the original changes:
.B ms_grid.snap
with
.B ms_grid.x
and
.B ms_grid.y
set to
.BR GRID ,
and
.B gr.fp_draw_ms
pointed at a routine that draws a
.B GrRect
instead of an arrow.
Plotted points therefore land only on multiples of five.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "left button"
.TP
.B "mouse move"
Move the snapped cursor
.TP
.B "left button"
Clear and exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/griddemo.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR mousedemo (1),
.IR wm (1)
